url: "https://github.com/ashleyxly/PVMark"
abstract: "PVMark is a plugin based on zero-knowledge proof (ZKP) that enables the watermark detection process to be publicly verifiable by third parties without disclosing any secret key. It is developed for three representative watermarking schemes (KGW, SynthID-Text, Segment-Watermark) and implements multiple variants covering combinations of three hash functions (MiMC, Poseidon, Poseidon2) and four ZKP protocols (Groth16, PlonK, halo2, Nova)."
